Z||000002||Spektrum-87GT||08-27-2001||06:18 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.colorshift.com" TARGET=_blank>www.colorshift.com</A> <BR>i guess the technical term for it is chromaflux paint. Its the kind that changes color. There are two different kinds too. The expensive stuff.... and the cheap stuff... trust me, you can tell the difference. if it looks like crap, its the cheap stuff(less than 100 bucks a gallon) and if it makes your jaw drop, its the expensive stuff($300/pint)||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||08-27-2001||06:31 PM||||the one ive used is chromillusion. has particles in it that refract the lite. It changes colors depending on direction lite hits it from. one side may look red, other side blue, back green, front yellow etc etc.||||reg||1
